{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VdvUGJkgABNHq5oDaJd1jB","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"About Our Ratings & Reviews [2025]\",\"url\":\"https://educationdata.org/about-our-ratings-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Survey - Speaker Deck\",\"url\":\"https://speakerdeck.com/harukiabe/corl-2025-survey\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150\"},{\"title\":\"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found some relevant information, though the results primarily cover NeurIPS 2025 and CoRL 2023 rather than specific 2025 CoRL guidelines:\n\n**Scoring Rubric (from similar AI conference guidelines):**\n\nThe NeurIPS 2025 reviewer guidelines use a scoring system that includes: Strong Accept (6 points) for technically flawless papers with groundbreaking impact; Accept (5 points) for technically solid papers with high impact; Borderline accept (4 points) for solid papers where acceptance reasons outweigh rejection reasons; Borderline reject (3 points) for solid papers where rejection reasons outweigh acceptance reasons; and Reject (2 points) for papers with technical flaws and weak evaluation.\n\n**CoRL 2023 Context:**\n\nThe search results show CoRL's reviewer guidelines build on ICML and NeurIPS guidance and are highly recommended, suggesting they follow similar frameworks.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results do not contain specific information about CoRL 2025's official reviewer guidelines, scoring rubric, or acceptance rate. To get the most current and accurate information for CoRL 2025, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 conference website or contacting the organizers directly.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f610776-11c8-4d04-b7bf-e42114d5f5d3","uuid":"481367ea-ac00-4a72-a2c4-6a25555771e0","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:31.345Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric acceptance rate","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013fi3LzzS8U7TPr7D6aMxbw","content":[{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"About Our Ratings & Reviews [2025]","url":"https://educationdata.org/about-our-ratings-reviews"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Survey - Speaker Deck","url":"https://speakerdeck.com/harukiabe/corl-2025-survey"},{"title":"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701"},{"title":"The AI Review Lottery: Widespread AI-Assisted Peer Reviews Boost Paper   Scores and Acceptance Rates","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.02150"},{"title":"Development and Validation of a Scoring Rubric for Editorial Evaluation of Peer-review Quality: A Pilot Study","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11000557/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found some relevant information, though the results primarily cover NeurIPS 2025 and CoRL 2023 rather than specific 2025 CoRL guidelines:\n\n**Scoring Rubric (from similar AI conference guidelines):**\n\nThe NeurIPS 2025 reviewer guidelines use a scoring system that includes: Strong Accept (6 points) for technically flawless papers with groundbreaking impact; Accept (5 points) for technically solid papers with high impact; Borderline accept (4 points) for solid papers where acceptance reasons outweigh rejection reasons; Borderline reject (3 points) for solid papers where rejection reasons outweigh acceptance reasons; and Reject (2 points) for papers with technical flaws and weak evaluation.\n\n**CoRL 2023 Context:**\n\nThe search results show CoRL's reviewer guidelines build on ICML and NeurIPS guidance and are highly recommended, suggesting they follow similar frameworks.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results do not contain specific information about CoRL 2025's official reviewer guidelines, scoring rubric, or acceptance rate. To get the most current and accurate information for CoRL 2025, I recommend checking the official CoRL 2025 conference website or contacting the organizers directly."],"durationSeconds":5.630274344000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ERbmrNJCgh6adtpouGNQyh","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CoRL 2026. However, the search results don't contain a specific detailed \"reviewer guidelines review form\" page for CoRL 2026. Here's what I found:\n\n**Available Information:**\n\nThe search shows that papers may be submitted through OpenReview via the link at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference, which is likely where the review form would be located once the review process begins.\n\n**Related Guidelines:**\n\nFor context, I found information from past CoRL conferences. Submissions for CoRL 2024 were evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, and reviewers evaluated relevance (whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, is evaluated in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested).\n\n**Reciprocal Review Requirements:**\n\nAll submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer, and they are qualified if they have at least one accepted publication at a previous robotics (CoRL/ICRA/IROS/RSS) or learning conference (ICLR/NeurIPS/ICML) or equivalent journal.\n\nFor the most current and specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, I recommend checking the OpenReview page directly or visiting the main CoRL 2026 website at corl.org.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f610776-11c8-4d04-b7bf-e42114d5f5d3","uuid":"62e19588-6b3e-42fd-8291-0b179b96bbd3","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:32.741Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_013RxP4hq3gLMbSsMYTT7wyd","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https:/