{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011GUmuvMgGabkuR5xE95c8v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring scale acceptance criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page. Here's what I found:\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and make reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nThe guidelines also emphasize that beating state-of-the-art results does not necessarily guarantee acceptance if the paper does not provide novel perspectives, insights, or sufficient knowledge advancement.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific details about the numerical scoring scale or explicit acceptance criteria thresholds for CoRL 2023. For more detailed information about the scoring scale and specific acceptance criteria, you may want to visit the official CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page directly at https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f610776-11c8-4d04-b7bf-e42114d5f5d3","uuid":"201c6ca9-9080-4d9d-ae05-07d8b0bcabcd","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:20:42.237Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring scale acceptance criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BB4G8UTnpNShEthY4cNB71","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2023%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page. Here's what I found:\n\nCoRL papers are required to include a limitations section. Reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation, while obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and reflected in scores.\n\nReviewers should be constructive and concrete, courteous and respectful, start with positive aspects, suggest improvements, and make reviews as informative and substantiated as possible.\n\nThe guidelines also emphasize that beating state-of-the-art results does not necessarily guarantee acceptance if the paper does not provide novel perspectives, insights, or sufficient knowledge advancement.\n\nHowever, the search results do not contain specific details about the numerical scoring scale or explicit acceptance criteria thresholds for CoRL 2023. For more detailed information about the scoring scale and specific acceptance criteria, you may want to visit the official CoRL 2023 Reviewer Guidelines page directly at https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines."],"durationSeconds":5.3386702710000025}}
