most extreme collapse: Goal Δ=0.691 (exit R² drops to −0.004), Spatial Δ=0.302.\n55\t- TracVLA trained shows moderate-to-large collapse across all 4 suites (Δ=0.138–0.294).\n56\t- OpenVLA Long trained is an outlier: Δ=0.004 (near-zero collapse), suggesting representations remain stable through exit layers.\n57\t- Untrained Δ values are uniformly small (0.009–0.076), confirming collapse is training-induced.\n58\t\n59\t**L1 attention (instruction-dominant heads):**\n60\t- TracVLA untrained: 32/32 instruction-dominant across all 4 suites — Phi-3's pretrained attention is already instruction-biased before fine-tuning.\n61\t- TracVLA trained: slightly reduced (27–30/32), suggesting fine-tuning repurposes some heads away from instruction-only attending.\n62\t- OpenVLA Object: 24/32 in both trained and untrained — no change from fine-tuning on this suite.\n63\t- OpenVLA Long: dramatic shift — 14/32 trained vs 25/32 untrained — fine-tuning heavily reorganizes attention for Long suite.\n64\t- NORA (16-head model): 12–14/16 instruction-dominant, similar between trained/untrained.\n65\t\n66\t**Counterfactual sensitivity (trained):**\n67\t- \"empty\" is the top condition for 5/6 available trained settings; OpenVLA Long is the exception with \"shuffled\" on top.\n68\t- TracVLA shows consistently high d values (1.2–1.5), indicating strong instruction sensitivity post-training.\n69\t- OpenVLA Long has notably weak CF sensitivity (d=0.45–0.56), possibly related to the near-zero R² collapse.\n70\t\n71\t**Counterfactual sensitivity (untrained):**\n72\t- \"empty\" is universally the top condition across all untrained models.\n73\t- Cosine distances are much smaller for untrained models (0.004–0.569), with OpenVLA Object being an outlier at 0.569.\n74\t- Consistent ordering: empty > shuffled > wrong > para in most cases.\n75\t\n76\t## Data Provenance\n77\t\n78\t| Cell | Source File |\n79\t|------|------------|\n80\t| OpenVLA Object trained R² | `libero_object/action_r2_probing.json` |\